From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: blissfulgit <blissfulgit@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 13:45:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] Bluetooth: hci: ignore default link policy rejection

The Unisoc UWE5621/UWE5622 Wi-Fi + BT combo used on many Amlogic TV boxes
answers HCI_OP_WRITE_DEF_LINK_POLICY with "Invalid HCI Command Parameters"
(0x12). hci_sync then fails the entire controller initialization and the
adapter can never be brought up:

  Bluetooth: hci0: Opcode 0x080f failed: -22
  Can't init device hci0: Invalid argument (22)

The controller is otherwise fine (reset succeeds, valid BD_ADDR is
reported), so log the rejection and keep going.
---
 net/bluetooth/hci_sync.c | 11 ++++++++---
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

--- a/net/bluetooth/hci_sync.c
+++ b/net/bluetooth/hci_sync.c
@@ -4352,8 +4352,15 @@
 
 	cp.policy = cpu_to_le16(link_policy);
 
-	return __hci_cmd_sync_status(hdev, HCI_OP_WRITE_DEF_LINK_POLICY,
-				     sizeof(cp), &cp, HCI_CMD_TIMEOUT);
+	/* Some controllers (e.g. Unisoc UWE5621/UWE5622) reject this with
+	 * "Invalid HCI Command Parameters" and would otherwise abort the
+	 * whole controller init. They work fine without it.
+	 */
+	if (__hci_cmd_sync_status(hdev, HCI_OP_WRITE_DEF_LINK_POLICY,
+				  sizeof(cp), &cp, HCI_CMD_TIMEOUT) < 0)
+		bt_dev_warn(hdev, "controller rejected default link policy, ignoring");
+
+	return 0;
 }
 
 static int hci_read_page_scan_activity_sync(struct hci_dev *hdev)
